# Milestone 5: Synthesis & Sharing

#### Milestone 5 is the unit’s project shareout milestone. Students finalize their Responsible AI Use Guides, test them with both AI and peers, and prepare to defend their recommendations publicly. Across Lessons 9 and 10, students refine products using mixed feedback and then synthesize evidence into a defended position about how humans should use AI.

## Milestone 5 Overview

#### **Lesson 9** is a Build Knowledge → Develop practice day where students iterate on their guides using AI stress tests and peer review to strengthen clarity, evidence, and audience fit.

#### **Lesson 10** is a Develop & Critique / Culminating lesson where students defend a claim about how humans should interact with AI and submit their final projects.

## 🧩 Project Progress

#### By the end of Milestone 5, students will finalize and submit their Responsible AI Use Guides and complete a short defended position (The Final Verdict) that cites unit evidence.
